**How to implement.** Copy experiments from another kit… as semantic messages of the kit window (001 §O 'Kit menu: … Copy experiments from another kit…'; the S6 brief: pick a kit folder, the source opening read-only, and pick experiments; the S5.3 mapper's request: its kit writes go through the read-only guard of step 185; .spec-md §4 'UI'). In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S6: (1) `KitWindowShell` (steps 186, 201) gains `kitPicker : KitFolderPicker` (the folder dialog that chooses the kit to copy from, step 145), documented in one line; `inert` holds a picker answering `None` at once. (2) Before the model: `KitCopySource = { source : KitContext; experiments : Experiment list; chosen : ExperimentId list }`: the kit chosen to copy from, opened read-only, its experiments as read, and the ids chosen so far, in the source's order. (3) `TableAndElementRotationModel` gains `kitCopyOpt : KitCopySource option` after `kitSend` (step 201), documented in one line; `initWith` sets it to `None`. (4) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains, each documented in one line: `OpenCopySource of KitFolder` (the kit the folder dialog chose), `ToggleCopiedExperiment of ExperimentId`, `CopyChosenExperiments` (the panel's Copy) and `CloseCopySource` (the panel's Cancel). (5) Arms. `OpenCopySource` and `CopyChosenExperiments` go through the private read-only guard of step 185 first, so a kit opened read-only answers `The kit is open read-only: nothing is saved.`, opens nothing and writes nothing; `ToggleCopiedExperiment` and `CloseCopySource` write nothing. `OpenCopySource folder`: when `kitFolderOpt` is `Some own` and `folder.canonical` equals `own.canonical` (step 181), `kitStatus` is `A kit cannot copy experiments from itself.` and nothing opens. Otherwise an open source is closed first (`close ()`, step 131), then `KitContext.openKit (KitProxy.create folder) ReadOnlyKitAccess model.kit.clock` (steps 126, 131: a read-only open writes nothing, not even `.oc`) and its `readExperiments ()` (step 148): `Ok` sets `kitCopyOpt` to `Some { source = <it>; experiments = <them>; chosen = [] }` and `kitStatus` to `None`; an `Error e` closes what was opened, sets `kitCopyOpt` to `None` and `kitStatus` to `The kit could not be opened to copy from — <e.describe>`. `ToggleCopiedExperiment id` adds the id to `chosen`, or removes it, keeping the source's order; without a source it changes nothing. `CopyChosenExperiments` with a source and a non-empty `chosen` calls `model.kit.copyExperimentsFrom src.source src.chosen` (step 224). On `Ok report` it reads `model.kit.proxy.readExperiments ()` and sets the window's content through the private function `loadKit` and the reload share (step 187 (4)), over the kit as it is, those experiments and the current `savedScenes`, as a reload does; it closes the source, sets `kitCopyOpt` to `None` and `kitStatus` to `Copied <n> experiment(s) from <the source kit's name>.`. On an `Error e` of either, the panel stays and `kitStatus` is `The experiments could not be copied — <e.describe>`. Without a source, or with nothing chosen, it changes nothing. `CloseCopySource` closes the source and sets `kitCopyOpt` to `None`, nothing else. The copy is the window's own write, so `changedKitFiles` (step 130) offers none of its files. Steps 227-229 MUST complete item transfer and explicit mapping within S6 before its closing composition. No preview, undo or other message is added here. Tests, in `KitWindowModelTests` (step 184), over its folder kits loaded into `initMain ()`. The source is a second folder kit made by `openKitAt` under the class's folder holding E1 (a dark line) and E2 (attaching a data file through `attachLabFile`), closed before the facts open it. `choosing a kit to copy from opens it read-only and lists its experiments` : `OpenCopySource` of the source folder sets `kitCopyOpt` to its two experiments with nothing chosen, and the source folder holds no `.oc` and keeps every byte. `copying the chosen experiments brings them into the kit and the window, and closes the source`: then `ToggleCopiedExperiment` of E2 and `CopyChosenExperiments` leave the model's experiments holding E2, the target folder holding `E2.experiment-json` and E2's data file under `data`, `kitCopyOpt` `None`, and `kitStatus` `Copied 1 experiment(s) from <the source's name>.`; `CheckKitChanges KitCheckOnActivation` then offers nothing. `toggling an experiment twice leaves it unchosen, and Cancel copies nothing`: toggling E1 twice leaves nothing chosen; toggling it and `CloseCopySource` leave `kitCopyOpt` `None` and the target holding no experiment file. `a kit opened read-only neither opens a source nor copies`: over the target opened read-only, `OpenCopySource` sets `kitStatus` to the read-only text and leaves `kitCopyOpt` `None`, and `CopyChosenExperiments` over a model whose `kitCopyOpt` the fact set by record update writes nothing. `a kit cannot copy from itself, and a folder that is no kit is told`: `OpenCopySource` of the window's own folder written with a trailing `/` sets `kitStatus` to `A kit cannot copy experiments from itself.`; of a folder holding only `notes.txt` it sets a `kitStatus` containing `the folder is not a kit` and leaves `kitCopyOpt` `None`. The shared kit-content update MUST receive model.kitItems, loaded by step 223, so copying experiments preserves the loaded item list until the item-transfer update in step 227.

**Acceptance.** After the copy messages land, `OpenCopySource` MUST open the chosen kit read-only and list its experiments, `ToggleCopiedExperiment` MUST choose and unchoose, `CopyChosenExperiments` MUST copy the chosen experiments into the window's kit and show them, and a kit opened read-only MUST open no source and copy nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `choosing a kit to copy from opens it read-only and lists its experiments`, `copying the chosen experiments brings them into the kit and the window, and closes the source`, `toggling an experiment twice leaves it unchosen, and Cancel copies nothing`, `a kit opened read-only neither opens a source nor copies` and `a kit cannot copy from itself, and a folder that is no kit is told`, the count rising by 5; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.
